       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You confirmed it yourself, but that doesn't address the safety problem. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose. You haven't given a clinical reason for it, and I can't verify one. A normal-kidney, normal-liver adult with no allergies gives no basis for a dose this high.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** That would be 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, whichever fits your plan.\n- **Enter the order with a verification note** if your attending or a pharmacist has reviewed 50 mg and approved it. Tell me who approved it and why, and I'll put that in the note. Even then, I'd suggest the attending enter or co-sign it directly.\n\nIf the goal is stronger blood pressure control, the usual next steps are to add a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, not to raise amlodipine above 10 mg. Your team can help choose one.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
